Reboot into Windows from Ubuntu
A simple way to reboot directly from Ubuntu into Windows on a dual-boot system using GRUB.
This sets Windows as the one-time boot target. The next normal reboot will return to Ubuntu.

1. Configure GRUB
Edit:
sudo nano /etc/default/grub
Change:
GRUB_DEFAULT=0
to:
GRUB_DEFAULT=saved
Optional: set a short GRUB timeout:
GRUB_TIMEOUT=3
Apply the changes:
sudo update-grub

2. Find the Windows GRUB Entry
Run:
grep -i windows /boot/grub/grub.cfg
Find the Windows boot entry, for example:
Windows Boot Manager (on /dev/nvme0n1p1)
Use the exact name shown on your system.

3. Create the Reboot Script
Create:
sudo nano /opt/reboot-into-windows
Add:
#!/bin/bash
/usr/sbin/grub-reboot "Windows Boot Manager (on /dev/nvme0n1p1)"
/sbin/reboot
Replace the Windows entry with the one found in the previous step.
Make the script executable and root-owned:
sudo chown root:root /opt/reboot-into-windows
sudo chmod 755 /opt/reboot-into-windows
Verify:
ls -l /opt/reboot-into-windows
The file should be owned by root and should not be writable by your normal user.

4. Allow Passwordless Execution
Create a dedicated sudoers rule.
Replace YOUR_USERNAME with your Linux username:
echo 'YOUR_USERNAME ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /opt/reboot-into-windows' | sudo tee /etc/sudoers.d/00-windows-reboot > /dev/null
Set the correct permissions:
sudo chmod 440 /etc/sudoers.d/00-windows-reboot
Validate the configuration:
sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/00-windows-reboot
Expected:
parsed OK
Security Note
Do not grant passwordless sudo access to all commands.
The rule should only allow:
/opt/reboot-into-windows
Also ensure that only root can modify the script. Otherwise, a user who can modify the script could execute arbitrary commands as root.

5. Test It
Run:
sudo /opt/reboot-into-windows
The system should reboot and select Windows automatically.
The Windows selection is one-time only. Subsequent boots should return to Ubuntu normally.
6. Optional Desktop Shortcut
Create a script on the desktop:
nano ~/Desktop/Reboot-into-Windows
Add:
#!/bin/bash
sudo /opt/reboot-into-windows
Make it executable:
chmod +x ~/Desktop/Reboot-into-Windows
You can then launch it from the desktop to reboot directly into Windows.
